Source patch for the GNU build layer only -- os/unix/wrapper.c, os/unix/fsys.c.

The last of the engine's warnings under GCC 13, none of them fatal under
GCC 14, fixed so the build is warning-free and the next one stands out:

  #endif SCCS / #endif SYS5 (five) -- K&R-era trailing labels, now comments.

  system(sccs_get(name)) (three, fsys.c) and write(2, ...) (three,
    wrapper.c's error()) -- glibc marks both warn_unused_result, and GCC
    ignores a (void) cast for that attribute on purpose, so the result is
    assigned and then dropped, with the reason next to it. The system()
    calls are Sun's auto-`sccs get` on an obsolete file, reachable only
    with -u, which this build never passes; error() writes to stderr on the
    way to exit. Nothing to do with either result.

  getwd(buf) -> getcwd(buf, MAXPATHLEN+1) (fsys.c s_getwd) -- the buffer is
    malloc(MAXPATHLEN+1) two lines up, so this is the same call with the
    bound glibc's deprecation and ld's "dangerous" note are about. Same
    return convention (buf or NULL).

Applied last, after printf-widths.patch, by build/obp/gnu/engine/Makefile to a
staged copy; src/obp is never touched.

